# Centralized Brains: Codex Rules
1. Read the global framework rules at `~\.agent-brains\GLOBAL_AGENT.md`.
2. This workspace's project is `DevilDogTG/DMNSN.Templates.NugetLibrary` (derived from `git remote get-url origin` at
   onboarding). Re-run the onboard script if the remote changes.
3. Read the workspace directives at `~\.agent-brains\projects\DevilDogTG/DMNSN.Templates.NugetLibrary\AGENT.md`.
4. Use `~\.agent-brains\projects\DevilDogTG/DMNSN.Templates.NugetLibrary\memory\` for project context.
5. Always write plans to `~\.agent-brains\projects\DevilDogTG/DMNSN.Templates.NugetLibrary\plan\` BEFORE writing code.

No agent state belongs in this repo. Only these entry points and `docs/adr/` live here.

## Agent Brains Skill Invocation

Treat `sk-<id>` as an Agent Brains framework skill invocation. These are shared framework skills,
not provider-native Codex skills. Resolve them by reading the first matching file in this order:

1. `~\.agent-brains\projects\DevilDogTG/DMNSN.Templates.NugetLibrary\skills\<id>\<id>.md`
2. `~\.agent-brains\profiles\<active-profile>\skills\<id>\<id>.md`
3. `~\.agent-brains\skills\<id>\<id>.md`

Use the active profiles listed in `~\.agent-brains\projects\DevilDogTG/DMNSN.Templates.NugetLibrary\AGENT.md`. Strip YAML
frontmatter, execute the `## Procedure` section, and do not rely on the generated skill registry as
the procedure source.

On the first user message of a new Codex session, run `sk-session-start` before handling the user's
task. If a user explicitly writes any `sk-*` token, that explicit skill invocation wins.


## Automatic Skill Routing

When the user's request clearly matches a session workflow, execute the matching framework skill as if
they had typed the explicit `sk-...` token.

Use this v1 routing table:
- First user message in a new session, "start session", "resume work", "pick up where we left off"
  -> `session-start`
- "summarize this session", "what did we do?", "give me a recap"
  -> `session-summary`
- "end session", "close session", "we're done", "continue later", "handover"
  -> `session-end`

Rules:
- Only auto-route when the intent is unambiguous.
- Prefer the least side-effecting skill that satisfies the request.
- Do not route recap-only requests to `session-end`.
- If the user's wording is ambiguous, ask instead of guessing.
- If the user explicitly writes an `sk-*` token, that explicit invocation wins.
